  "narration": "Let's rank every Porsche Boxster generation. At number four, we have the 718 Boxster 982, the turbocharged innovation. Kicking off in 2016 at $56,000 with 300 horsepower, it brought in turbocharged engines, sharper suspension tuning, a modern infotainment system, and a stiffer chassis. Then comes the Boxster 987, which turned up the volume on refinement and style. Released in 2005 at $43,500, its 240 horsepower came with cleaner styling, improved proportions, and a much more luxurious cabin. Today, it\u2019s valued at about $56,000, showing its steady appreciation. The second spot is for the original, the Boxster 986. It roared onto the scene in 1996, priced at $39,980 with 204 horsepower. This model saved Porsche with its iconic fried egg headlights, mid-engine layout, and classic Porsche badge. Nowadays, it\u2019s a nostalgic favorite with values around $23,000. Finally, taking the top spot is the Boxster 981, the modern classic. Launched in 2012 at $49,500 with 265 horsepower, it\u2019s all about that naturally aspirated engine and hydraulic steering. It stands as the driver\u2019s choice with its wider stance and aggressive styling, now worth $91,000 for its timeless appeal. Which Boxster generation stands out to you\u2014the revolutionary 718 or the classic 986?",
